    <detaileddescription>
<para>Cache Replication for High-Availability Deployments</para>
<para>Provides an interface for propagating cache writes, invalidations, and full snapshots to standby replica nodes so that a replica can serve cached data immediately after a primary failure.</para>
<para>Design principles:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Transport-agnostic: the caller supplies a concrete ICacheReplicationListener implementation (in-process, TCP, gRPC, …).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Graceful degradation: a failing replica is marked UNHEALTHY and skipped until it recovers; the primary continues serving requests.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Consistent with the existing themisdb::replication::IReplicationListener interface style used in include/replication/replication_manager.h.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
